\section*{Summary}
This report searches for positive integer solutions of
\[
21n^3+19=(12x+7)k
\]
with
\[
n\geq 10^{20}.
\]
Because no upper bound on \(n\), \(x\), or \(k\) was specified, the unrestricted problem has infinitely many solutions. For example, every even \(n\) gives
\[
 k=1,\qquad x=\frac{7n^3+4}{4}.
\]
So the finite computational part of this report uses the explicit search range
\[
0\leq x\leq 500,\qquad n\geq N:=10^{20}.
\]
Within this \(x\)-range the report gives a complete congruence description of all solutions with \(n\geq N\). It also lists the solutions in the finite window
\[
10^{20}\leq n<10^{20}+1000.
\]

The computation found:
